# Keep canonical text at LF regardless of core.autocrlf. The checker compares
# generated references as exact bytes, and POSIX shebangs need LF to execute
# directly. Zellij and Windows editors accept LF. The exception is zj.cmd:
# cmd.exe can misread labels and `goto`
# in a batch file with LF-only line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.wasm  binary
# Preserve exact upstream license text, including its final blank line.
licenses/*.txt whitespace=-blank-at-eof
